<title>USA: Integrated Process withdraws offering.</title>
<headline>Integrated Process withdraws offering.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integrated Process Equipment Corp said Friday it has withdrawn its proposed offering of three million common shares.</p>
<p>All of the shares were to be offered by the company.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe the market price at this time does not reflect the true value of IPEC's business opportunity and product position,&quot; said chief executive Sanjeev Chitre.</p>
<p>The stock offering represented a long term financing opportunity.  However, in view of protecting shareholder value, management and the board decided to forego the offering under the present market conditions, he explained.</p>
<p>He said &quot;the withdrawal of this offering does not alter the company's strategy.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
